      "note": "Re-judged 2026-10-19 (independent auditor, after 990744517c and f8ca08b2ca). Section 3: \"The link-local address shall be included in the Next Hop field if and only if the BGP speaker shares a common subnet with the entity identified by the global IPv6 address carried in the Network Address of Next Hop field and the peer the route is being advertised to.\" Tested is 'only if the BGP speaker shares a common subnet with the entity identified by the global IPv6 address carried in the Network Address of Next Hop field and the peer the route is being advertised to.'; Gap is 'The link-local address shall be included in the Next Hop field if'; Producer internal/component/bgp/reactor/link_scope.go::linkLocalNextHop. Annotation unchanged. linkLocalNextHop gained a linkLocalCondition argument: linkLocalConditionFor returns the RFC 2545 joint condition (sharesNextHopSubnet via holdsCommonSubnet) for every family except AFI 2/SAFI 128, which takes RFC 4659 Section 3.2.1.1's peer-only condition (owner decision 2026-10-19). For RFC 2545 families the decision is unchanged, and the ThirdParty/Unspecified router branch still returns no address, so the Gap is exactly as recorded. TestRFC2545ReceivedPairSubnetConditions now splits the VPN-IPv6 global-off-link case to keep the pair (RFC 4659), while the unicast cases still assert exact 32-octet keep only when both entities share one prefix and an exact 16-octet trim when either is off-link; the VPN subcases test RFC 4659 under an RFC 2545 tag but do not weaken the unicast proof. TestRFC2545StaticLabeledIPv6LinkLocalCommonSubnet (SAFI 4) asserts the exact 32-octet field on the common subnet and the 16-octet global off it. No discrimination record for RFC2545-3-3 is reported unverified by ./le rfc check. Scoped evidence only; zero whole-requirement credit.",
